A_669 - There is a Christian saying: "Blessed are the poor in spirit, for theirs is the kingdom of heaven." In my opinion, the exact opposite is true: the poor in spirit are unhappy both in life and in death, and those who did not concern themselves with finding spirit while alive (I explained how to do this in element A_034) will suffer the consequences until they do find it. Furthermore, the prayer "Grant them eternal rest, O Lord, and let perpetual light shine upon them; may they rest in peace" is also inaccurate in my view, since eternal rest cannot be granted after a temporary life—no matter how arduous that life may have been.